<title>HONG KONG: MAS unit 5-yr bond raised to 40 bln yen.</title>
<headline>MAS unit 5-yr bond raised to 40 bln yen.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following Euro-Yen bond, announced earlier by arranger Daiwa Securities (HK) Ltd, has been increased to 40 billion yen from 30 billion yen.</p>
<p> BORROWER    MALAYSIA AIRLINES CAPITAL (L) LTD</p>
<p> GUARANTOR   MALAYSIAN AIRLINE SYSTEM BERHAD (MAS)</p>
<p> AMOUNT	40 BLN YEN  COUPON     2.55 PCT MATURITY  29.MAY.02</p>
<p> TYPE     EURO-YEN BOND  ISS PRICE  PAR	LAUNCH    20.MAY.97</p>
<p> PUTS	  *	     CALLS	NONE     REPLIES   --</p>
<p> LISTING     --	    REPAYMENT  BULLET   DENOMS    --</p>
<p> RATING	A+ NIS	SALE LMTS  --	 PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> HOME CTRY   MALAYSIA    GOV LAW    --	 PAY DATE  29.MAY.97</p>
<p>MGT LEVELS AND FEES -- NOT DISCLOSED</p>
<p>ARRANGER  DAIWA SECURITIES (HK) LTD</p>
<p> NOTES     *THE ISSUE CAN BE PUT IF THE MINISTER OF FINANCE</p>
<p>	     OR THE GOVERNMENT OF MALAYSIA CEASES TO HOLD THE ONE</p>
<p>	     SPECIAL REDEEMBALE PREFERENCE SHARE OF THE GUARANTOR.</p>
<p>	     A MANAGEMENT GROUP IS BEING FORMED</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6960</p>
</text>
